/F2 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 742 Tm (Warehouse Incident SOP) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 714 Tm (Document number: OPS-SOP-014) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 700 Tm (Owner: Operations) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 686 Tm (Version 7, effective 1 June 2026) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 672 Tm (Audience: Operations) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 644 Tm (1. Scope) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 626 Tm (This procedure applies to every AcmeCorp warehouse. An incident is any event that) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 612 Tm (injures a person, damages goods or equipment, or could have done so. Near misses are) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 598 Tm (incidents.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 570 Tm (2. Immediate actions) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 552 Tm (Section 2 is for the first person on the scene.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 532 Tm (1. Make the area safe. Stop nearby equipment and keep people away.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 518 Tm (2. If anyone is injured, call the site first aider on the internal emergency number 555.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 504 Tm (For a serious injury call the public emergency number first.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 490 Tm (3. Tell the shift supervisor at once.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 476 Tm (4. Do not move damaged goods or equipment unless they are a danger, so the scene can be) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 462 Tm (recorded.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 434 Tm (3. Supervisor actions) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 416 Tm (1. Take charge of the scene and confirm that Section 2 has been done.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 402 Tm (2. Take photographs of the area, the goods and any equipment involved.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 388 Tm (3. Collect the names of everyone who was present.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 374 Tm (4. Move damaged goods to the quarantine area and label them with the incident number.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 360 Tm (5. Decide the severity level using Section 4.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 332 Tm (4. Severity levels) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 84 314 Tm (- Level 1: near miss, or damage under 1,000 EUR, with no injury.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 84 300 Tm (- Level 2: damage of 1,000 EUR or more, or an injury needing first aid only.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 84 286 Tm (- Level 3: an injury needing medical treatment, a fire, a chemical spill, or damage) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 93 272 Tm (above 25,000 EUR.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 244 Tm (5. Reporting times) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 84 226 Tm (- All levels: the supervisor files an incident report in the operations system within) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 93 212 Tm (24 hours.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 84 198 Tm (- Level 2: the site manager is told before the end of the shift.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 84 184 Tm (- Level 3: the site manager and the Head of Operations are told within 1 hour, by) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 93 170 Tm (phone. The area stays closed until the site manager reopens it.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 142 Tm (6. Forklift and equipment incidents) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 124 Tm (Any equipment involved in an incident is taken out of service and tagged. It returns to) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 110 Tm (service only after an inspection by maintenance. The operator does not drive again until) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 96 Tm (the supervisor has spoken to them and recorded it.) Tj
ET
