/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 742 Tm (7. Damaged customer goods) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 724 Tm (The supervisor records the order numbers of damaged goods in the incident report.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 710 Tm (Customer service is told the same day so that replacements can be arranged.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 682 Tm (8. Follow-up) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 664 Tm (For Level 2 and Level 3 incidents the site manager holds a review within 5 working days) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 650 Tm (and records the cause and the corrective actions. Actions are tracked in the operations) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 636 Tm (system until closed.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 608 Tm (9. Records) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 590 Tm (Incident reports are kept for 5 years.) Tj
